{
  "case_id": "2009-08-1553",
  "document_hash": "eb26074753cab8d8d2e14ad0ba1abf38f53113d3cd8200ebcdb95f6b8842482a",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1553",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "eb26074753cab8d8d2e14ad0ba1abf38f53113d3cd8200ebcdb95f6b8842482a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-eb26074753ca-0000-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: We\u2019ll hear argument first this morning in Case 08-1553, Kawasaki Kisen Kaisha, Ltd. v. Regal-Beloit Corporation, and the consolidated case."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1553",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "eb26074753cab8d8d2e14ad0ba1abf38f53113d3cd8200ebcdb95f6b8842482a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-eb26074753ca-0000-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: Are you taking -- are you taking a position different than the U.S., that it applies to exports but not imports? I think the -- the Solicitor General's position is that it doesn't apply to any import or export."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Kawasaki Kisen Kaisha Ltd. (Petitioner)",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1553",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "eb26074753cab8d8d2e14ad0ba1abf38f53113d3cd8200ebcdb95f6b8842482a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-eb26074753ca-0000-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "From its enactment in 1906 until very recently, it has been settled law for a century that the Carmack Amendment does not apply to the inland leg of an import through shipment."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Kawasaki Kisen Kaisha Ltd. (Petitioner)",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1553",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "eb26074753cab8d8d2e14ad0ba1abf38f53113d3cd8200ebcdb95f6b8842482a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-eb26074753ca-0000-0006",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 7,
        "start": 7
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The simplest way to resolve this case is that I believe even Respondents would concede that for Carmack to apply, you need a receiving carrier that is a rail carrier. \"K\" Line is the receiving carrier here, and they are not a rail carrier."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States (amicus curiae)",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1553",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "eb26074753cab8d8d2e14ad0ba1abf38f53113d3cd8200ebcdb95f6b8842482a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-eb26074753ca-0000-0004",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. YANG: Mr. Chief Justice, and may it please the Court: I\u2019d like to address a few of the questions that have come up already. Justice Sotomayor, you asked what Supreme Court decision addresses the receiving carrier. There\u2019s a series of decisions which address receiving carriers and the nature of the receiving carrier as the initial carrier that receives goods from the shipper."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Kawasaki Kisen Kaisha Ltd. (Petitioner)",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1553",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "eb26074753cab8d8d2e14ad0ba1abf38f53113d3cd8200ebcdb95f6b8842482a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-eb26074753ca-0000-0005",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the practical consequence of that is that true through bills of lading -- unity of responsibility in one shipper under consistent terms for the entire voyage -- will become impossible in foreign trade."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Yang",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1553",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "eb26074753cab8d8d2e14ad0ba1abf38f53113d3cd8200ebcdb95f6b8842482a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-eb26074753ca-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Regarding the geographic scope of Carmack on the current text, we believe that the current text, which is reproduced in the petition appendix at 69a -- if you look at the combination of both the first and the third sentences of Carmack, we believe that that reproduces the historic scope as encompassing only domestic transportation, purely domestic transportation, and transportation to an adjacent foreign country when it's an export."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1553",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "eb26074753cab8d8d2e14ad0ba1abf38f53113d3cd8200ebcdb95f6b8842482a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-eb26074753ca-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: Excuse me. What -- what are you referring to now?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1553",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "eb26074753cab8d8d2e14ad0ba1abf38f53113d3cd8200ebcdb95f6b8842482a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-eb26074753ca-0001-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 29,
        "start": 29
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: Did the Ninth Circuit pass on that argument?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Frederick",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1553",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "eb26074753cab8d8d2e14ad0ba1abf38f53113d3cd8200ebcdb95f6b8842482a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-eb26074753ca-0001-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 30,
        "start": 30
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "they are liable for the loss; the Carmack Amendment applies to their receipt of the property; and the train derailment which was caused by their negligence comes within the plain terms of the Carmack Amendment."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Carmack Amendment",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1553",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "eb26074753cab8d8d2e14ad0ba1abf38f53113d3cd8200ebcdb95f6b8842482a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-eb26074753ca-0001-0005",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 31,
        "start": 31
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "\"Failure to issue a receipt or bill of lading does not affect the liability of a rail carrier.\""
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1553",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "eb26074753cab8d8d2e14ad0ba1abf38f53113d3cd8200ebcdb95f6b8842482a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-eb26074753ca-0001-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 34,
        "start": 34
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: What are you arguing, estoppel?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Frederick",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1553",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "eb26074753cab8d8d2e14ad0ba1abf38f53113d3cd8200ebcdb95f6b8842482a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-eb26074753ca-0001-0008",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "We didn't make that argument. Our argument was that, based on the functions and them holding themselves out to be a rail carrier, which they have done, they qualify under the normal ICC method of determining rail carrier."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Frederick",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1553",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "eb26074753cab8d8d2e14ad0ba1abf38f53113d3cd8200ebcdb95f6b8842482a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-eb26074753ca-0001-0009",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "\"K\" Line is the receiving rail carrier when it transfers from the international ocean carriage corporation to the American multimodal transportation operation and gets the goods from the Port of Long Beach up to Los Angeles, and then treat UP, Union Pacific, as the delivering rail carrier."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1553",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "eb26074753cab8d8d2e14ad0ba1abf38f53113d3cd8200ebcdb95f6b8842482a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-eb26074753ca-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "In what capacity -- \"K\" Line is the contracting party with Union Pacific. Under what contract could the shipper sue Union Pacific?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1553",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "eb26074753cab8d8d2e14ad0ba1abf38f53113d3cd8200ebcdb95f6b8842482a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-eb26074753ca-0002-0002",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Union Pacific removed this case from State court to Federal court, the Federal question was they said: There is a Carmack Amendment claim being asserted against us."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1553",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "eb26074753cab8d8d2e14ad0ba1abf38f53113d3cd8200ebcdb95f6b8842482a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-eb26074753ca-0002-0003",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And when they -- when they sought to transfer the case from California to New York, they did so on the basis of the convenience of 28 of the 32 witnesses to their train derailment being American citizens."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1553",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "eb26074753cab8d8d2e14ad0ba1abf38f53113d3cd8200ebcdb95f6b8842482a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-eb26074753ca-0002-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Do we have a brief here?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1553",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "eb26074753cab8d8d2e14ad0ba1abf38f53113d3cd8200ebcdb95f6b8842482a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-eb26074753ca-0002-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 54,
        "start": 54
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Is that enough to make the shipper a railroad?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Counsel",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1553",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "eb26074753cab8d8d2e14ad0ba1abf38f53113d3cd8200ebcdb95f6b8842482a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-eb26074753ca-0003-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 59,
        "start": 59
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "This case was decided on a rule 12(b)(3) motion to dismiss for improper venue, and the lower courts have made clear, sensibly, that if you are confronted with a forum selection motion to dismiss, you are required to at least come forward with any factual disputes that you think need to be resolved before the district court can grant or deny that motion."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1553",
      "confidence": 0.96,
      "document_hash": "eb26074753cab8d8d2e14ad0ba1abf38f53113d3cd8200ebcdb95f6b8842482a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-eb26074753ca-0003-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 59,
        "start": 59
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "How -- how do you get out of the language that says that a rail carrier providing transportation \u201cshall issue a receipt\u201d for property it receives?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Ballenger",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1553",
      "confidence": 0.94,
      "document_hash": "eb26074753cab8d8d2e14ad0ba1abf38f53113d3cd8200ebcdb95f6b8842482a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-eb26074753ca-0003-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 60,
        "start": 60
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Under the definitions, a rail carrier is a party providing railroad transportation."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1553",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "eb26074753cab8d8d2e14ad0ba1abf38f53113d3cd8200ebcdb95f6b8842482a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-eb26074753ca-0003-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 61,
        "start": 61
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Now just give me how -- what I would write in the opinion that would in fact -- because what they did here, the ship, is it took a container and put it on the train. Okay? So that's inter-service equipment. What's the language that does it your way?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Ballenger",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1553",
      "confidence": 0.94,
      "document_hash": "eb26074753cab8d8d2e14ad0ba1abf38f53113d3cd8200ebcdb95f6b8842482a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-eb26074753ca-0003-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 61,
        "start": 61
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "A party providing rail common carrier transportation, the scope of the -- of that transportation is defined to include a container. But that doesn't mean that everyone who owns a container is -- meets the first part of the definition of providing railroad transportation."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1553",
      "confidence": 0.0,
      "document_hash": "eb26074753cab8d8d2e14ad0ba1abf38f53113d3cd8200ebcdb95f6b8842482a",
      "evidence_id": "unavailable-eb26074753ca-62",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
